      "question": {
        ":question/id": "b65ef168-8dfa-5b78-99a4-fc82c2fdef11",
        ":question/problem": "Given that\n\n$$\nS=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 & -8 \\\\ -1 & -8 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nwhich of the following elementary row operations makes $a_{11}=0$?",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Of the given options, we consider the row operation\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-{R}_{2}.\n$$\n\nAt the requested entry, this gives\n\n$$\na_{11}=-1+(-1)\\cdot (-1)=0.\n$$\n\nApplying the above row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S &=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 & -8 \\\\ -1 & -8 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\qquad {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-{R}_{2} \\\\ &\\sim \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 12 & -8 \\\\ -1 & -8 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-{R}_{2}.\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
