        ":question/problem": "Given that\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 12 \\\\ -3 & -6 & -5 \\\\ -6 & -7 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nwhich of the following elementary row operations makes $a_{33}=0$?",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Of the given options, we consider the row operation\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1}.\n$$\n\nAt the requested entry, this gives\n\n$$\na_{33}=-3+\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)\\cdot (12)=0.\n$$\n\nApplying the above row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T &=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 12 \\\\ -3 & -6 & -5 \\\\ -6 & -7 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\qquad {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1} \\\\ &\\sim \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 12 \\\\ -3 & -6 & -5 \\\\ - \\frac{23}{4} & - \\frac{33}{4} & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1}.\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
