        ":question/problem": "Given that\n\n$$\nS=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -5 & -6 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nwhich of the following elementary row operations makes $a_{23}=0$?",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Of the given options, we consider the row operation\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}\u2194{R}_{3}.\n$$\n\nThe entry in row $3$, column $3$ is $0$. Switching rows $2$ and $3$ therefore makes $a_{23}=0$.\n\nApplying the above row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S &=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -5 & -6 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\qquad {R}_{2}\u2194{R}_{3} \\\\ &\\sim \\begin{bmatrix}-9 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -5 & -6 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}\u2194{R}_{3}.\n$$",
